  "aiContextParagraph": "Recent reports have shed light on the involvement of Chinese technology during Operation Sindoor, a military event occurring in 2022. According to findings cited in new coverage, three Chinese surveillance satellites were utilized to observe India's western coastline, with a particular emphasis on the Gujarat region. These satellites reportedly tracked key military installations and civilian infrastructure, including the Jamnagar refinery owned by Reliance, by optimizing their orbital paths. This development follows recent assessments from a United States panel, which alleged that China provided strategic backing to Pakistan during the operation. The panel claims that this support was intended to monitor and curb India's rising regional profile. These revelations add a significant geopolitical dimension to the historical account of the operation, highlighting the role of external intelligence and surveillance support in regional tensions.",
